Subject: Re: [PATCH v3 2/4] media: qcom: camss: vfe-4-1: program the RDI write master buffer size

On an LG Fx0 (MSM8226, CAMSS behind the IOMMU) with IMX179 and IMX132,
this also fixes two RDI streams at once on VFE0. Without it the first
write master reports bus overflow (IRQ_STATUS_1 = 0x200) continuously,
about 225k VFE interrupts per second, until CPU0 stalls (RCU stall
report). With it, both streams run at full rate (30 and 14 fps) with
about 90 VFE interrupts per second. Tested on 6.18.64 with 4/4.

Tested-by: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com> # LG Fx0 (MSM8226)
